# s4-golden-replay core wiring

## 1. Cargo: native/core/crates/mixdog-browser-engine/Cargo.toml, section [dev-dependencies]
The two integration tests (tests/golden.rs, tests/contract.rs) are a separate crate: they read `FakeHost` through the feature
`test-support` and need the tools' specs and `regex`. Add under [dev-dependencies], after the existing `mixdog-testkit` and `tokio` lines:

    # Every workspace crate this crate's tests build, with its test-only features, so a test build has one feature set
    # whatever packages are selected (D:\mixdog-build\tools\unify-test-features.py).
    mixdog-browser-engine = { path = ".", features = ["test-support"] }
    mixdog-tools = { workspace = true, features = ["policy-observer"] }
    regex = { workspace = true }

`policy-observer` is the test-only feature every other crate's dev-dependency on mixdog-tools names (one feature set per test
build). mixdog-tools brings further workspace crates into this crate's test build (mixdog-ai, mixdog-spawn, ...): after applying,
run `D:\mixdog-build\tools\unify-test-features.py <native/core> --write` so their lines with their test-only features are added too.

New workspace-crate edge: mixdog-browser-engine -> mixdog-tools (dev only; mixdog-tools does not depend on the engine, no cycle).
regex is already in Cargo.lock (1.13.1); Cargo.lock needs the three new entries in the mixdog-browser-engine package (regenerate --locked offline).

## 2. No module line, no protocol row, no SERVICE_PENDING change.

## 3. The fixture the test needs and does not find yet
tests/golden.rs reads native/core/fixtures/desktop-host/browser-engine-transcript.jsonl (recorded by the integrator in s4-harness-rebase-a:
the JSONL rows FakeHost::from_transcript_str reads, every host/browser/* call of the 50 steps of browser-golden.json in script order, the pushes
between them). Until it is recorded `cargo test -p mixdog-browser-engine --test golden` FAILS (it does not skip): the fixture! read panics on the
missing file. The transcript may hold the run's real origin (http://127.0.0.1:PORT) or the placeholder <ORIGIN>; the test accepts both.
